  "scope": "Windows/Linux each pass twenty native suites, ten background repetitions, four hidden background GL contexts and 3321 installed Python checks, zero failure/error/skip. Eleven new Python cases cover native editor Apply across UInt8/UInt16, whole/active masks and T/C/Z scopes, submission-time settings/recording, paired history, strict replay/rebind validation and disabled floating controls. Expanded native desktop fixtures cover an actual Apply button, all-Z independent pixel expectations, busy/job reporting, Undo/Redo, worker-only blocked virtual IO, global foreign-thread/job-ID cancellation, panel/source closure, stale display and eventual reservation release. Linux builds fingerprint the native compiled source mirror and run a byte-verified native snapshot of 5467 test/config/fixture files. Disposable module origins match retained qualified installs. Scratch is archived with CRC and per-member SHA verification before exact owned-path removal. Original 99 requirement/status triples and existing build/test registrations are preserved. This is scalar desktop Apply integration, not full ImageJ/Fiji or G057/platform/resource acceptance.",
